  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $14.18B (-1.6% 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/11/19/trump-s-democratic-sec-pick-suggests-tokenization-policy-deserves-full-rule-process\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trump&#x27;s Democratic SEC pick suggests tokenization policy deserves full rule process</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-11-18-ondo-to-launch-tokenized-anthropic-stock-on-ipo-day-443482\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ondo to launch tokenized Anthropic stock on IPO day</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/11/19/singapore-settles-usd77-5-million-tokenized-bill-sale-in-local-cbdc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Singapore settles $77.5 million tokenized bill sale in local CBDC</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/podcasts-and-videos/podcast/who-decides-which-chains-count-as-public-or-cosmos-zenith-injective\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Who Decides Which Chains Count as Public? | Cosmos, Zenith, Injective</a> (The Defiant).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
